WEBVTT

00:22:59.845 --> 00:23:03.147
being the person that was willing

00:23:03.171 --> 00:23:07.417
and seeming to the others empowered enough

00:23:07.441 --> 00:23:08.942
to change the norm.

00:23:09.322 --> 00:23:11.576
But they would just be
spinning and spinning,

00:23:11.600 --> 00:23:14.014
it's like, "We can't,
but we should, but we can't."

00:23:14.038 --> 00:23:15.252
Where did that come from?

00:23:15.276 --> 00:23:17.507
I was like, "Guys,
it's totally OK, just do it,

00:23:17.531 --> 00:23:19.252
if it's not OK I'll take the heat."

00:23:19.276 --> 00:23:20.483
And it was always OK.

00:23:20.507 --> 00:23:24.336
And I feel like, when things got stuck,

00:23:24.360 --> 00:23:26.512
that's a lot of the stuff
that was happening,

00:23:26.536 --> 00:23:27.900
it was these cultural norms,

00:23:27.924 --> 00:23:30.012
and you couldn't even ask somebody,